<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">ARA General Belgrano</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1938">1938</a>–<a href="/years/1982">1982</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">ARA General Belgrano was an Argentine light cruiser, built in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> as USS Phoenix, which survived the attack on Pearl Harbor and was sold to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> in 1951. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/falklands-war">Falklands War</a> it was torpedoed by the British submarine HMS Conqueror on 2 May 1982, with the loss of 323 lives, nearly half of Argentina's deaths in the conflict.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ara-general-belgrano.jpg" alt="ARA General Belgrano" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ARA_General_Belgrano_underway.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
